#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-release.md
msgid "CAP-RELEASE.1"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-release.md
msgid "MUST"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-release.md
msgid "For each release unit, expected subjects (from an external register) balance against confirmed results; any duplicate, orphan, missing subject, pending identity or absent register reads BLOCKED.{1}*Example:* A school's register lists 30 learners; 29 have confirmed results and one has none, so the school reads BLOCKED until the missing one is found or recorded as absent."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-release.md
msgid "Fixtures for each blocking condition read BLOCKED; a balanced unit reads CLEAR."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-release.md
msgid "CAP-RELEASE.2"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-release.md
msgid "Results release only on CLEAR, and a release is recorded as the point after which changes are new versions."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-release.md
msgid "A change after release creates a new version and leaves the released one intact."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-release.md
msgid "CAP-RELEASE.3"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-release.md
msgid "The register is read through an adapter and frozen as an immutable snapshot per sitting; corrections are deterministic, evented operations, never ad-hoc edits."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-release.md
msgid "Each sitting references one snapshot; register corrections appear as events."
msgstr ""

